# Measured after implementation (v0.2.13 candidate, 2026-11-05), against the
#   published v0.2.12 binary from crates.io:
#   judge_reach_test 19 of 19; full suite 771 passed; mutants 71 of 71 (RE-M1..M8
#   each killed by its named fixture); clippy -D warnings silent.
#   Label-free: 20 VIOLATED, 12 confirmed, 28 printed, 0 failed (unchanged).
#   Iglu: ADDITION VIOLATED 5, 3 confirmed, 0 failed (unchanged). SchemaStore
#   replay.sh: PASS.
#   Verdict moves, v0.2.12 to v0.2.13 (full per-pair lists in reach-moves/):
#     SchemaStore 819 pairs: HOLDS to NOT EVALUATED (unchecked_change) 521; HOLDS
#       kept 73; VIOLATED kept 41; NOT EVALUATED (unjudged_construct) kept 184.
#     Iglu 146 pairs: HOLDS to NOT EVALUATED 25; HOLDS kept 69; VIOLATED kept 48;
#       NOT EVALUATED kept 4.
#     AsyncAPI 7 minor pairs, tag neutralized: HOLDS to NOT EVALUATED 7.
#   No witness was added or removed on any corpus: VIOLATED counts identical.
#   MANIFEST labels are untouched: they record whether a commit breaks, not what
#   the judge said, and NOT EVALUATED claims neither.
#   Existing fixtures that encoded a false pass, amended in the engine commit:
#     judge_contracts_test OPEN_WIDER (a typed property added to an open object,
#     called a widening; {"nick":1} breaks). Replaced by a true widening.
